    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d413">

                <pb facs="0516" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/852a Supp.: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                            All Diplomatic Missions in Latin
                    America</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-25T16:00:00-05:00">January 25, 1933—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Colombian Government addressed note to this Government,<anchor n="59"
                        xml:id="d413-f1"/> as a signatory of Kellogg Pact, asking it to call Peru’s
                    attention to her obligations under that Pact. Secretary of State in a long
                    telegram today to the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Peru set forth the views
                        <pb facs="0517" n="429" xml:id="pg429"/> of this Government regarding the
                    situation in the light of the correspondence exchanged between Colombia and Peru
                    and urged Peruvian Government to abide by the commitments undertaken by it in
                    Pact of Paris and the declaration of August 3d last and that it accept the
                    solution proposed by the Brazilian Government for a peaceful settlement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
